'''Bauhinian''' (bâ-hin′i-a̤n), ''a.'' Relating to the Swiss anatomist and botanist Gaspard Bauhin (1560–1624).—{{smaller|'''Bauhinian valve, valvula Bauhini,''' the ileocæcal valve. See ''ileocæcal.''}}

'''bauk''' (bâk), ''n.'' A Scotch form of ''balk''<sup>1</sup>.

'''bauld''' (bâld), ''a.'' A Scotch form of ''bold.''

'''bauldricke†''', ''n.'' See ''baldric.''
